1
00:00:32,365 --> 00:00:39,330
FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

2
00:00:41,041 --> 00:00:44,711
YEAR 2026

3
00:00:46,504 --> 00:00:47,338
Now,

4
00:00:47,422 --> 00:00:51,259
everyone, let's raise a glass to
our artist, who gave us such a wonderful

5
00:00:51,342 --> 00:00:52,385
performance today.

6
00:00:53,636 --> 00:00:55,346
Congratulations are also in order…

7
00:00:55,430 --> 00:00:58,516
To Jae-in on this first step as Pi-o's
new manager.

8
00:01:06,691 --> 00:01:08,943
I'm glad everything wrapped up without
issue.

9
00:01:09,527 --> 00:01:10,904
Still,
do you have any idea how

10
00:01:10,987 --> 00:01:11,946
much you scared me?

11
00:01:12,864 --> 00:01:14,824
You took ten years off of my life.

12
00:01:15,408 --> 00:01:17,202
We all owe it to Jae-in, of course.

13
00:01:17,827 --> 00:01:18,661
You know…

14
00:01:19,162 --> 00:01:22,332
knowing you're Pi-o's manager gives
me so much peace of mind.

15
00:01:23,166 --> 00:01:25,418
You don't have to tell me how tough
it must be.

16
00:01:25,502 --> 00:01:28,088
- I feel bad for you.
- You're not wrong

17
00:01:28,171 --> 00:01:29,089
Ms. Kang.

18
00:01:29,589 --> 00:01:31,716
I only put up with it cos I'm a big fan.

19
00:01:31,800 --> 00:01:32,801
Ufff…

20
00:01:33,384 --> 00:01:34,219
Honestly,

21
00:01:34,302 --> 00:01:37,263
how many people get to make money with
their favorite thing?

22
00:01:37,347 --> 00:01:38,181
Know what I mean?

23
00:01:38,264 --> 00:01:39,474
That's how I cope.

24
00:01:40,600 --> 00:01:43,561
Still,
if he ever gives me a real hard time,

25
00:01:43,645 --> 00:01:45,230
you'll scold him for me, won't you?

26
00:01:45,313 --> 00:01:46,606
Of course.

27
00:01:47,148 --> 00:01:49,109
How's the Esplanade show coming along?

28
00:01:49,609 --> 00:01:51,319
All seats are completely sold out,

29
00:01:51,820 --> 00:01:54,364
but there are additional requests for
VIP tickets,

30
00:01:54,447 --> 00:01:56,866
so we're negotiating with the Singapore
agency.

31
00:01:57,742 --> 00:01:59,285
Sorry, Excuse me for a moment.

32
00:01:59,369 --> 00:02:00,286
Okay.

33
00:02:04,332 --> 00:02:07,544
The time between the Vienna and Singapore
concerts is too tight.

34
00:02:12,882 --> 00:02:14,843
- Sorry 'bout that.
- Kang Pi-o?

35
00:02:17,345 --> 00:02:18,513
Hey, it's really you!

36
00:02:19,472 --> 00:02:20,306
Been a while.

37
00:02:21,182 --> 00:02:23,309
I've seen you on the news from
time to time.

38
00:02:23,393 --> 00:02:25,270
You know how I've been up to, right?

39
00:02:28,898 --> 00:02:31,234
What's up with that rumor about Choi
Jeong-yo?

40
00:02:32,235 --> 00:02:33,862
What exactly happened with that?

41
00:02:34,654 --> 00:02:36,906
I heard that you had something to do with
it.

42
00:02:41,911 --> 00:02:44,789
I see you're just as pathetic as you were
back in school.

43
00:02:45,373 --> 00:02:46,207
What?

44
00:02:59,387 --> 00:03:01,472
Since when has your pinky been like this?

45
00:03:03,474 --> 00:03:05,894
If you leave it like that, you're
gonna ruin it.

46
00:03:06,811 --> 00:03:08,897
Stop practicing and get it treated first.

47
00:03:15,195 --> 00:03:19,866
FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

48
00:03:20,575 --> 00:03:22,368
EPISODE 6

49
00:04:50,915 --> 00:04:51,749
Mm

50
00:04:53,334 --> 00:04:54,544
Guess where I am.

51
00:04:59,173 --> 00:05:00,008
Turn around.

52
00:05:03,386 --> 00:05:04,512
PI-O PI-O

53
00:05:04,595 --> 00:05:05,430
Ta-da.

54
00:05:06,973 --> 00:05:07,807
Ah…

55
00:05:08,516 --> 00:05:09,350
This is nice.

56
00:05:12,186 --> 00:05:13,021
I wonder…

57
00:05:13,104 --> 00:05:16,399
Why is it that I never get tired of
listening to you?

58
00:05:17,859 --> 00:05:21,321
You have no idea…
how glad I am that I became your manager.

59
00:05:23,614 --> 00:05:25,408
Can you stop saying things like that?

60
00:05:25,491 --> 00:05:26,617
It's not funny.

61
00:05:27,368 --> 00:05:28,661
What do you mean?

62
00:05:29,662 --> 00:05:31,539
How many people out there get to hear…

63
00:05:31,622 --> 00:05:33,291
a million-dollar performance

64
00:05:33,374 --> 00:05:35,960
without having to fight for a ticket
to the show?

65
00:05:40,548 --> 00:05:41,382
Hey,

66
00:05:42,258 --> 00:05:43,343
be honest with me.

67
00:05:44,344 --> 00:05:45,178
You actually…

68
00:05:46,637 --> 00:05:49,265
really like having me as your mm-manager,
don't you?

69
00:05:50,516 --> 00:05:53,436
- I do, yeah.
- You actually like it when I drop in…

70
00:05:54,270 --> 00:05:56,147
without telling you first, right?

71
00:05:56,230 --> 00:05:57,273
I do.

72
00:05:59,359 --> 00:06:00,193
Then,

73
00:06:00,693 --> 00:06:01,861
when are we getting married?

74
00:06:01,944 --> 00:06:02,945
I--

75
00:06:04,364 --> 00:06:07,033
Wow, aren't you tired of asking me that?

76
00:06:08,868 --> 00:06:09,702
Hey!

77
00:06:10,703 --> 00:06:13,039
Haven't I done enough
to win you over by now?

78
00:06:13,998 --> 00:06:17,085
Hey, you're not gonna brush me off by
saying you're married to your music,

79
00:06:17,168 --> 00:06:19,420
- are you?
- Oh, hey you figured it out.

80
00:06:20,296 --> 00:06:21,964
Ugh, What do I even see in him…

81
00:06:24,050 --> 00:06:25,051
Hey, wait up!

82
00:06:25,968 --> 00:06:26,803
Hurry.

83
00:06:33,684 --> 00:06:37,063
Now, let's ask some questions to the
star of this competition,

84
00:06:37,146 --> 00:06:38,898
and the most renowned pianist,

85
00:06:38,981 --> 00:06:40,441
Mister Pi-o Kang!

86
00:06:43,569 --> 00:06:44,529
Woot woot woot!

87
00:06:45,738 --> 00:06:48,533
Ever since the Harmonie Competition
nine years ago,

88
00:06:48,616 --> 00:06:52,745
you've been at the forefront of bringing
classical music to a wider audience

89
00:06:53,287 --> 00:06:55,998
with both undeniable skill and star
quality!

90
00:06:56,624 --> 00:06:57,458
Back then,

91
00:06:57,542 --> 00:07:00,086
you shocked everyone by
delivering an explosive

92
00:07:00,169 --> 00:07:02,338
performance even after breaking a nail.

93
00:07:02,922 --> 00:07:03,840
How did you do it?

94
00:07:04,924 --> 00:07:05,800
Back then,

95
00:07:06,384 --> 00:07:07,427
I was focused, so…

96
00:07:07,927 --> 00:07:09,720
I didn't feel any pain at all.

97
00:07:09,804 --> 00:07:11,973
The Harmonie Competition was a stage

98
00:07:12,765 --> 00:07:14,267
I dreamed of performing upon.

99
00:07:14,767 --> 00:07:16,144
And once I was there,

100
00:07:17,562 --> 00:07:19,188
pain in my finger didn't matter.

101
00:07:19,272 --> 00:07:20,314
Wow.

102
00:07:20,398 --> 00:07:24,402
What was even more astonishing was your
unique interpretation of the set piece.

103
00:07:24,485 --> 00:07:28,114
To make an interpretation like that and
deliver such a complete performance

104
00:07:28,197 --> 00:07:30,616
in just a week is no small achievement.

105
00:07:31,325 --> 00:07:34,454
How were you able to accomplish such a
difficult challenge?

106
00:07:36,038 --> 00:07:38,040
It definitely wasn't easy.

107
00:07:38,124 --> 00:07:39,625
The pressure was intense.

108
00:07:40,126 --> 00:07:41,794
I just focused on doing the best,

109
00:07:42,378 --> 00:07:43,838
and it led to a good result.

110
00:07:44,505 --> 00:07:47,091
I don't know if I could ever pull that
off again.

111
00:07:47,800 --> 00:07:50,887
Okay, now that nine years have
passed, I'd like to ask you a more

112
00:07:50,970 --> 00:07:52,305
sensitive question.

113
00:07:52,388 --> 00:07:56,184
At the time, the finalists must have been
deeply shaken by the loss of a fellow

114
00:07:56,267 --> 00:07:57,268
competitor.

115
00:07:57,768 --> 00:08:00,938
It remains an unhealed wound for
us on the committee as well.

116
00:08:01,481 --> 00:08:02,940
How did you overcome that?

117
00:08:03,524 --> 00:08:04,358
Uh…

118
00:08:05,151 --> 00:08:07,278
Um… It's been a very long time, but

119
00:08:07,778 --> 00:08:08,988
life goes on

120
00:08:09,071 --> 00:08:10,031
and music

121
00:08:10,114 --> 00:08:11,699
heals us all, right?

122
00:08:12,408 --> 00:08:16,245
For me,
music was my healing and my salvation.

123
00:08:17,121 --> 00:08:18,080
Come to think of it,

124
00:08:18,164 --> 00:08:20,958
you went to the same school as that
competitor, right?

125
00:08:23,586 --> 00:08:25,546
- Yes.
- Were you close?

126
00:08:29,133 --> 00:08:31,761
Uh-- No, we weren't that close.

127
00:08:45,525 --> 00:08:47,109
Good job out there, Kang Pi-o!

128
00:08:49,278 --> 00:08:50,196
These are yours.

129
00:08:50,738 --> 00:08:52,532
Gifts from your fans in Korea.

130
00:08:53,574 --> 00:08:55,034
They go all out, don't they?

131
00:09:01,832 --> 00:09:03,084
MESSAGES
NEW NOTIFICATION

132
00:09:04,752 --> 00:09:07,588
I found someone who says he spotted Mr.
Choi in Romania.

133
00:09:09,048 --> 00:09:09,882
Jae-in.

134
00:09:10,758 --> 00:09:12,760
- Excuse me…
- Mm-hmm.

135
00:09:21,769 --> 00:09:22,645
Hey, Mister Kang.

136
00:09:24,188 --> 00:09:25,690
All right, tell me everything.

137
00:09:26,315 --> 00:09:27,942
Who is this guy you found?

138
00:09:28,025 --> 00:09:30,403
Ah, well,
his name is Farid and he's a refugee.

139
00:09:31,028 --> 00:09:33,322
When I asked if he knew where Mister Choi
went,

140
00:09:33,406 --> 00:09:35,366
he demanded money for the info. So?

141
00:09:35,449 --> 00:09:38,452
- Should I pay him and see what he knows?
- Not yet.

142
00:09:38,995 --> 00:09:41,372
I'd like to go over there
and verify it myself.

143
00:09:45,918 --> 00:09:46,752
Oh…

144
00:09:47,336 --> 00:09:48,170
Let's go.

145
00:09:48,796 --> 00:09:51,799
Oh… I can't come to the party tonight.

146
00:09:51,882 --> 00:09:53,050
Why not?

147
00:09:53,759 --> 00:09:55,052
You said you'd come though.

148
00:09:55,136 --> 00:09:56,721
Don't make me go alone.

149
00:09:57,263 --> 00:09:58,389
I'm sorry, it's just…

150
00:09:59,265 --> 00:10:01,851
A professor I've been wanting to
meet for a while said he has some

151
00:10:01,934 --> 00:10:03,185
time for me tomorrow.

152
00:10:03,269 --> 00:10:04,854
But, I'll need to go to Münster.

153
00:10:04,937 --> 00:10:05,771
Hm…

154
00:10:06,397 --> 00:10:07,648
Guess it can't be helped.

155
00:10:09,400 --> 00:10:10,526
The promo party, though…

156
00:10:10,610 --> 00:10:11,527
You can't miss.

157
00:10:11,611 --> 00:10:14,113
We really need you there for that one.

158
00:10:14,905 --> 00:10:16,866
I know you do. Back soon, 'kay?

159
00:10:30,129 --> 00:10:31,922
Václav Havel Airport, please.

160
00:10:46,562 --> 00:10:47,396
Honey,

161
00:10:47,480 --> 00:10:48,314
MOM

162
00:10:48,397 --> 00:10:49,607
AS FOR ME, I GOT THE COMMITTEE
POSITION I MENTIONED THE OTHER DAY

163
00:10:49,690 --> 00:10:51,067
Smile when you take a bow.

164
00:10:51,150 --> 00:10:51,984
IT'S PROBABLY GOING TO BE QUITE A HASSLE

165
00:10:52,068 --> 00:10:53,319
You're not sick, are you?

166
00:11:03,120 --> 00:11:06,374
We will now begin the appointment
ceremony for new members of the National

167
00:11:06,457 --> 00:11:09,043
Culture and Arts Promotion Fund Steering
Committee.

168
00:11:11,128 --> 00:11:12,797
SHAPING THE FUTURE
THROUGH CULTURE AND ARTS

169
00:11:12,880 --> 00:11:16,592
You are hereby appointed as a member of
the Music Division of the National

170
00:11:16,676 --> 00:11:19,303
LOCATION: MAIN AUDITORIUM,
MINISTRY OF CULTURE, SPORTS, AND TOURISM

171
00:11:19,387 --> 00:11:22,306
Kim Tae-seong, Minister of
Culture, Sports, and Tourism.

172
00:11:29,313 --> 00:11:30,981
Seriously, You're unbelievable!

173
00:11:31,065 --> 00:11:34,860
How did you manage to beat everyone else
and snag a seat on the committee so

174
00:11:34,944 --> 00:11:35,986
quickly?

175
00:11:36,070 --> 00:11:36,904
I admire you…

176
00:11:36,987 --> 00:11:38,948
and not just cos we're friends.

177
00:11:39,031 --> 00:11:40,366
Oh, you're just saying that.

178
00:11:40,449 --> 00:11:41,951
I only got cos it was my turn.

179
00:11:43,244 --> 00:11:44,453
So, Ms. Committee Member,

180
00:11:44,537 --> 00:11:45,788
what's on your agenda?

181
00:11:45,871 --> 00:11:47,665
Oh, my duties start next week.

182
00:11:48,165 --> 00:11:49,166
Today,

183
00:11:49,250 --> 00:11:52,002
I'm just helping evaluate the
gifted school admissions.

184
00:11:53,003 --> 00:11:53,879
Really?

185
00:11:53,963 --> 00:11:56,716
Have you see any candidates there worth
recommending?

186
00:11:57,216 --> 00:11:58,676
I'm still a bit bitter…

187
00:11:58,759 --> 00:12:00,761
that Namu Productions got Park Sae-jin.

188
00:12:01,262 --> 00:12:04,098
I'll have to see how he does today.
How about Gam U-jin?

189
00:12:04,682 --> 00:12:05,766
He seems pretty good.

190
00:12:07,226 --> 00:12:08,644
Oh, Gam U-jin?

191
00:12:08,728 --> 00:12:10,938
What? You don't like him?

192
00:12:11,021 --> 00:12:12,940
Oh, I know he's talented,

193
00:12:13,482 --> 00:12:14,442
His looks, though…

194
00:12:15,651 --> 00:12:18,195
Hey, you need to pick a kid with
musical talent

195
00:12:18,279 --> 00:12:20,239
if you want an artist who can win
awards, I mean

196
00:12:20,322 --> 00:12:21,490
they're not actors.

197
00:12:22,491 --> 00:12:23,701
That's not how it works.

198
00:12:24,201 --> 00:12:25,202
A handsome kid,

199
00:12:25,286 --> 00:12:27,955
will sell tickets even if
their hands shake on stage.

200
00:12:28,497 --> 00:12:30,541
Music is eighty percent about looks.

201
00:12:31,375 --> 00:12:34,295
All right then, I'll let you know if
there's a decent candidate there today,

202
00:12:34,378 --> 00:12:35,296
just hang tight.

203
00:12:35,379 --> 00:12:37,089
Oh, you know I love you, right?

204
00:12:37,590 --> 00:12:39,508
I swear, what would I do without you?

205
00:12:40,134 --> 00:12:41,343
Ah, stop it.

206
00:12:42,762 --> 00:12:44,096
I'll call you later, 'kay?

207
00:12:49,977 --> 00:12:50,895
Mrs. Kim!

208
00:12:52,438 --> 00:12:54,523
I think the dry cleaners made a mistake.

209
00:12:54,607 --> 00:12:55,941
These clothes aren't mine.

210
00:12:56,567 --> 00:12:58,068
Oh, these are Ms. Yoon's old--

211
00:13:00,279 --> 00:13:01,113
Oh…

212
00:13:01,197 --> 00:13:03,783
Why haven't you gotten rid of the
clothes of someone who left this

213
00:13:03,866 --> 00:13:04,867
house five years ago?

214
00:13:04,950 --> 00:13:05,868
And of all places…

215
00:13:07,369 --> 00:13:09,121
Why would you hang them in my room?

216
00:13:09,205 --> 00:13:12,541
Well…
I would've taken them out if I'd known.

217
00:13:12,625 --> 00:13:13,584
Perhaps, Ms. Lee…

218
00:13:14,084 --> 00:13:15,961
noticed them in Mister Kang's room

219
00:13:16,045 --> 00:13:18,547
and mistook them for yours, and hung them
there.

220
00:13:21,091 --> 00:13:22,468
Throw them out immediately.

221
00:13:51,997 --> 00:13:53,916
As for me, Hyeon Seon-hwa, Lee Na-rae,

222
00:13:53,999 --> 00:13:55,125
2026 CHEONGUN MUSIC EDUCATION
APPLICATION FORM

223
00:13:55,209 --> 00:13:56,919
and Gam U-jin, look good.

224
00:13:57,461 --> 00:13:59,755
Uh, I think these three show the most
potential.

225
00:13:59,839 --> 00:14:01,799
And of the three, Gam U-jin seems, uh…

226
00:14:01,882 --> 00:14:03,843
to most closely fit the profile

227
00:14:03,926 --> 00:14:05,970
of the type of student we are looking
for.

228
00:14:06,053 --> 00:14:06,887
Excuse me.

229
00:14:07,388 --> 00:14:09,765
You said Gam U-jin - was your favorite?

230
00:14:10,975 --> 00:14:12,268
I don't know about him.

231
00:14:13,060 --> 00:14:14,520
He's a bit of a gamble.

232
00:14:14,603 --> 00:14:17,857
I know he seems very talented, but his
fundamentals are lacking.

233
00:14:17,940 --> 00:14:19,108
It's just…

234
00:14:19,942 --> 00:14:22,111
I worry he'll put style over substance.

235
00:14:22,611 --> 00:14:26,115
He makes mistakes because he started
playing later than the others, which

236
00:14:26,198 --> 00:14:27,032
is to be expected.

237
00:14:27,116 --> 00:14:28,868
And if we want - to find a prodigy

238
00:14:29,368 --> 00:14:31,161
shouldn't we look at their potential

239
00:14:31,245 --> 00:14:33,247
rather than the superficial aspects?

240
00:14:34,081 --> 00:14:35,374
Superficial, you say?

241
00:14:36,750 --> 00:14:39,461
Surely you know how crucial the
first year or two are in a young

242
00:14:39,545 --> 00:14:40,713
musician's development.

243
00:14:41,297 --> 00:14:43,883
Why should a taxpayer-funded institute
like ours…

244
00:14:44,383 --> 00:14:47,511
waste resources on a kid whose
fingers have already stiffened?

245
00:14:48,095 --> 00:14:50,556
I propose… rather than Gam U-jin…

246
00:14:51,515 --> 00:14:53,183
This one. Kim Hong-gyu.

247
00:14:54,560 --> 00:14:56,020
I'd put them forward instead.

248
00:15:07,823 --> 00:15:08,657
Hyun-soo!

249
00:15:14,371 --> 00:15:16,081
What was with that look all about?

250
00:15:17,333 --> 00:15:18,167
What?

251
00:15:18,959 --> 00:15:21,211
Did you not like the candidate I put
forward?

252
00:15:21,295 --> 00:15:22,421
No, I didn't like him.

253
00:15:24,298 --> 00:15:27,384
Is it right to let our history
influence a decision that'll affect a

254
00:15:27,468 --> 00:15:29,803
- child's future?
- What are you talking about?

255
00:15:30,804 --> 00:15:31,639
What,

256
00:15:32,264 --> 00:15:36,185
do you actually think that I rejected
Gam U-jin just to pick a fight with you?

257
00:15:43,400 --> 00:15:44,234
You're right.

258
00:15:45,486 --> 00:15:48,030
I wanted to see what your
reaction would be like.

259
00:15:48,864 --> 00:15:51,367
And that's what it took,
to get you to talk to me.

260
00:15:52,368 --> 00:15:54,370
How long will you treat me like this?

261
00:15:54,912 --> 00:15:58,207
Isn't it crazy,
that we only ended up like this, because…

262
00:15:58,290 --> 00:16:00,918
- somebody else got between us?
- No,

263
00:16:01,001 --> 00:16:02,920
it wasn't because of someone else.

264
00:16:05,381 --> 00:16:07,007
It's your fault we're like this.

265
00:16:07,925 --> 00:16:08,759
Enough.

266
00:16:17,601 --> 00:16:20,396
ROMANIA

267
00:16:28,362 --> 00:16:30,197
Ah! Hello.

268
00:16:30,280 --> 00:16:32,199
- May I help you?
- Ah, sorry.

269
00:16:33,033 --> 00:16:34,118
Ah…

270
00:16:34,201 --> 00:16:35,494
I've a question.

271
00:16:35,577 --> 00:16:36,996
Um…

272
00:16:37,079 --> 00:16:37,913
Let's see now…

273
00:17:10,863 --> 00:17:12,239
Uh… Mister Farid.

274
00:17:12,322 --> 00:17:13,240
Mm-hmm.

275
00:17:13,741 --> 00:17:17,619
You mentioned that three years ago,
you encountered another homeless man

276
00:17:17,703 --> 00:17:19,538
who played the piano well, right?

277
00:17:19,621 --> 00:17:21,373
Yeah. That's right.

278
00:17:21,457 --> 00:17:22,458
Yes, he says he did.

279
00:17:22,541 --> 00:17:24,001
Could you identify

280
00:17:25,335 --> 00:17:26,670
which of these men he was?

281
00:17:29,048 --> 00:17:29,882
Mmm

282
00:17:36,096 --> 00:17:37,431
Uh… This man here.

283
00:17:39,308 --> 00:17:41,310
How did you know
he was good at playing the piano?

284
00:17:41,393 --> 00:17:43,270
Did you see him play yourself?

285
00:17:43,353 --> 00:17:44,313
Um…

286
00:17:45,522 --> 00:17:46,982
He said, um…

287
00:17:47,066 --> 00:17:49,109
his dream was to be a pianist,

288
00:17:49,610 --> 00:17:50,694
but…

289
00:17:51,445 --> 00:17:54,031
- he was heartbroken that he could
- He says the man dreamt of being a

290
00:17:54,114 --> 00:17:55,657
- no longer pursue that dream.
- pianist, but was heartbroken as he

291
00:17:55,741 --> 00:17:57,034
- Because he couldn't use his right
- couldn't pursue it.

292
00:17:57,117 --> 00:17:58,410
Hand anymore…

293
00:17:59,036 --> 00:18:00,704
he couldn't use his right hand anymore.

294
00:18:00,788 --> 00:18:03,207
H- he couldn't use his
right hand anymore?

295
00:18:05,584 --> 00:18:07,461
Did he say why he couldn't use it?

296
00:18:07,544 --> 00:18:09,546
Why couldn't he use his right hand?

297
00:18:09,630 --> 00:18:10,798
Do you know why?

298
00:18:10,881 --> 00:18:11,799
Uh…

299
00:18:11,882 --> 00:18:12,925
He just said

300
00:18:13,425 --> 00:18:14,593
that he had hurt it.

301
00:18:15,094 --> 00:18:17,638
- He didn't say how he'd gotten hurt.
- Some kind of an injury,

302
00:18:17,721 --> 00:18:19,765
but he didn't tell him how it happened.

303
00:18:22,476 --> 00:18:24,728
Do you know where he went after you
saw him?

304
00:18:24,812 --> 00:18:26,063
Where did he go after that?

305
00:18:26,146 --> 00:18:28,440
Uh… Um, I'm sorry, but…

306
00:18:28,524 --> 00:18:30,400
I'm gonna need… A hit pretty soon.

307
00:18:30,484 --> 00:18:31,902
Could I have some money?

308
00:18:32,778 --> 00:18:34,446
He needs cash for his drug habit.

309
00:18:45,958 --> 00:18:47,334
I want you to be specific.

310
00:18:48,961 --> 00:18:50,629
Where did he say he was going?

311
00:18:50,712 --> 00:18:52,172
He want's you to be specific.

312
00:18:52,840 --> 00:18:54,883
Do you know where he might have gone?

313
00:18:55,509 --> 00:18:57,261
He said he was…

314
00:18:58,720 --> 00:19:00,305
gonna board a ship…

315
00:19:00,806 --> 00:19:02,850
and return to his hometown or something.

316
00:19:03,809 --> 00:19:06,478
He said… he was going to Constanța.

317
00:19:06,562 --> 00:19:08,605
He said he caught a ship to return to
his hometown.

318
00:19:08,689 --> 00:19:11,066
He said he missed his mom, that she
was waiting for him to come home.

319
00:19:11,150 --> 00:19:12,359
Said he missed his mom.

320
00:19:12,985 --> 00:19:13,986
He mentioned…

321
00:19:14,736 --> 00:19:15,821
going to see his mom?

322
00:19:31,920 --> 00:19:33,338
You're looking for the pianist.

323
00:19:33,422 --> 00:19:35,048
He hasn't been here for two weeks.

324
00:19:35,132 --> 00:19:37,926
But, I saw him two weeks ago, Yeah,
he was definitely here.

325
00:19:38,010 --> 00:19:39,970
This guy…? No - this one's not him.

326
00:19:40,053 --> 00:19:41,138
But… this guy.

327
00:19:41,221 --> 00:19:42,181
He was here.

328
00:19:42,264 --> 00:19:43,682
This man. He was here.

329
00:19:44,725 --> 00:19:45,559
This is him.

330
00:19:45,642 --> 00:19:46,977
That man was Korean,

331
00:19:47,060 --> 00:19:48,478
but he wasn't a pianist.

332
00:19:49,146 --> 00:19:50,439
What is he saying?

333
00:19:50,522 --> 00:19:51,857
That the man was Korean,

334
00:19:53,108 --> 00:19:54,026
but not a pianist.

335
00:20:14,755 --> 00:20:18,008
How much longer are we gonna
keep shooting in the dark like this?

336
00:20:18,717 --> 00:20:20,302
It's been five years already.

337
00:20:21,511 --> 00:20:23,347
After all this time,
shouldn't you have at least

338
00:20:23,430 --> 00:20:24,431
found a clue by now?

339
00:20:27,267 --> 00:20:29,853
It's not like I'm asking you to catch the
kidnappers.

340
00:20:29,937 --> 00:20:31,855
I just wanna know if he's dead or not.

341
00:20:33,607 --> 00:20:34,775
Is it really that hard?

342
00:20:36,109 --> 00:20:38,111
Look, even Interpol couldn't locate him.

343
00:20:38,820 --> 00:20:40,197
You think it's easy for me?

344
00:20:42,115 --> 00:20:44,868
What then? Do you… wanna stop looking?

345
00:20:47,329 --> 00:20:49,539
Look, my reputations on the line
too, 'kay?

346
00:20:50,040 --> 00:20:53,085
I mean, Interpol has already concluded
that Mister Choi is dead.

347
00:20:53,168 --> 00:20:55,712
And we've searched everywhere we
could think of.

348
00:20:55,796 --> 00:20:57,965
The only thing we haven't
found is his body.

349
00:20:58,048 --> 00:21:00,759
Mister Choi's chances of being alive
are next to zero.

350
00:21:04,638 --> 00:21:06,848
What exactly is it that you want to
confirm?

351
00:21:08,558 --> 00:21:10,018
Is it that Mr. Choi is alive?

352
00:21:10,978 --> 00:21:12,020
Or that he is dead?

353
00:21:24,741 --> 00:21:26,994
- Cheers!
- Here's to us!

354
00:22:15,375 --> 00:22:17,586
What exactly is it that you want to
confirm?

355
00:22:18,628 --> 00:22:20,088
Is it that Mr. Choi is alive?

356
00:22:21,131 --> 00:22:22,090
Or that he is dead?

357
00:22:42,694 --> 00:22:44,488
- Mm?
- Hey,

358
00:22:44,571 --> 00:22:45,697
where are you?

359
00:22:46,365 --> 00:22:48,867
The party's over and you even
didn't show.

360
00:22:49,785 --> 00:22:51,036
Oh, sorry.

361
00:22:52,913 --> 00:22:53,747
Guess I forgot.

362
00:22:54,498 --> 00:22:55,665
Have you been drinking?

363
00:23:01,380 --> 00:23:02,214
A little…

364
00:23:02,798 --> 00:23:04,007
Where are you right now?

365
00:23:19,564 --> 00:23:20,399
Ugh…

366
00:23:21,316 --> 00:23:22,234
Hey, Kang Pi-o!

367
00:23:23,652 --> 00:23:24,528
Hey wake up.

368
00:23:25,153 --> 00:23:26,029
What's going on?

369
00:23:27,864 --> 00:23:28,698
Oh…

370
00:23:30,075 --> 00:23:30,951
You're here.

371
00:23:31,034 --> 00:23:32,536
Um… Did something happen?

372
00:23:34,204 --> 00:23:36,623
Why did you drink so many beers all
on your own?

373
00:23:38,333 --> 00:23:39,209
Nothing happened.

374
00:23:41,128 --> 00:23:41,962
Hey

375
00:23:42,629 --> 00:23:44,172
Hey… Pi-O!! Careful!

376
00:23:46,091 --> 00:23:48,635
Seriously,
What the hell's gotten into you?

377
00:23:49,928 --> 00:23:51,596
- Ugh…
- Keep walking.

378
00:23:51,680 --> 00:23:53,348
- Ugh…
- Okay?

379
00:23:53,432 --> 00:23:54,433
We're almost there.

380
00:23:55,725 --> 00:23:57,394
- Ugh…
- Oh…

381
00:23:57,477 --> 00:23:59,187
No. I'm fine.

382
00:23:59,729 --> 00:24:00,564
You can go.

383
00:24:01,106 --> 00:24:02,190
I can walk on my own.

384
00:24:03,692 --> 00:24:04,943
You're going to get hurt.

385
00:24:07,988 --> 00:24:08,947
Where's your key?

386
00:24:25,005 --> 00:24:25,839
Jae-in.

387
00:24:27,674 --> 00:24:28,842
I'm sorry.

388
00:24:30,260 --> 00:24:33,221
Could you please just stay with me
until I fall asleep?

389
00:24:34,931 --> 00:24:35,765
What?

390
00:24:38,351 --> 00:24:41,104
You won't even accept how I feel,
but still want me to watch you

391
00:24:41,188 --> 00:24:42,022
fall asleep?

392
00:24:43,356 --> 00:24:44,524
You're so selfish.

393
00:24:47,402 --> 00:24:48,820
Because you're the only one…

394
00:24:52,115 --> 00:24:53,617
that I can trust.

395
00:24:58,872 --> 00:24:59,706
Yeah, I know.

396
00:25:01,166 --> 00:25:03,376
Do you still have a lot of trouble
sleeping?

397
00:25:04,628 --> 00:25:05,462
Mm-hmm.

398
00:25:06,880 --> 00:25:08,340
I just want to clear my head

399
00:25:11,718 --> 00:25:13,011
and sleep for a while.

400
00:25:14,971 --> 00:25:16,723
I told you to stop working so hard.

401
00:25:17,974 --> 00:25:19,309
You need to get some rest.

402
00:25:20,727 --> 00:25:22,604
How about cutting some of your shows?

403
00:25:23,188 --> 00:25:24,689
You could take a sabbatical.

404
00:25:24,773 --> 00:25:25,774
How's that?

405
00:25:29,861 --> 00:25:30,695
Maybe.

406
00:25:32,030 --> 00:25:33,156
Give yourself a break.

407
00:25:34,074 --> 00:25:34,991
Just relax

408
00:25:35,534 --> 00:25:37,160
You're doing a great job.

409
00:25:39,204 --> 00:25:40,038
Pi-o.

410
00:25:41,831 --> 00:25:43,708
I'd like to get something off my chest.

411
00:25:43,792 --> 00:25:44,751
Can I?

412
00:25:45,961 --> 00:25:46,795
Sure…

413
00:25:49,422 --> 00:25:50,632
Well, it's just that…

414
00:25:52,801 --> 00:25:55,178
You know that I really like you a lot,
right?

415
00:25:57,305 --> 00:25:58,139
You know, right?

416
00:25:59,432 --> 00:26:00,267
I know.

417
00:26:01,601 --> 00:26:02,435
No, you don't.

418
00:26:03,270 --> 00:26:04,229
You have no idea.

419
00:26:09,526 --> 00:26:10,360
The truth is…

420
00:26:13,947 --> 00:26:15,198
Every time I told you…

421
00:26:16,116 --> 00:26:18,785
I made it sound like I was joking
and laughed it off…

422
00:26:20,787 --> 00:26:23,248
but actually, I meant every word.

423
00:26:42,851 --> 00:26:45,061
Just don't be in pain, Kang Pi-o.

424
00:27:14,382 --> 00:27:17,594
I found out the man who kidnapped
Mister Choi was just released from

425
00:27:17,677 --> 00:27:18,678
Rezina Penitentiary.

426
00:27:23,767 --> 00:27:25,435
What did you mean with that text?

427
00:27:25,977 --> 00:27:27,687
You mean you know where he is?

428
00:27:27,771 --> 00:27:31,566
MOLDOVA

429
00:27:38,657 --> 00:27:40,116
His name is Andrei Ceban.

430
00:27:41,242 --> 00:27:42,744
He's from Transnistria.

431
00:27:42,827 --> 00:27:43,912
He's forty-eight.

432
00:27:44,788 --> 00:27:46,039
A former mercenary.

433
00:27:46,665 --> 00:27:48,500
He was serving time for assault.

434
00:27:49,292 --> 00:27:50,585
They just let him out.

435
00:27:51,544 --> 00:27:55,215
Man, no wonder I couldn't find a trace of
him, the bastard was locked up.

436
00:27:57,676 --> 00:27:59,636
By the way, can I ask you something?

437
00:27:59,719 --> 00:28:02,472
Ah, you told me not to ask any questions,
so I haven't…

438
00:28:03,390 --> 00:28:04,557
But Mister Kang,

439
00:28:04,641 --> 00:28:07,227
why are you trying so hard to find Mister
Choi?

440
00:28:07,310 --> 00:28:09,104
Even his family would've given up.

441
00:28:12,273 --> 00:28:14,234
Is he really all that important to you?

442
00:28:14,901 --> 00:28:15,777
This Mister Choi?

443
00:28:41,928 --> 00:28:43,430
Hey, hey, hey, hey. Where are you going?

444
00:28:43,513 --> 00:28:44,848
Oh, uh, Andrei Ceban here?

445
00:28:45,640 --> 00:28:47,308
- And your name?
- Ah, Vogel.

446
00:28:47,392 --> 00:28:49,102
Ah, that guy. Inside.

447
00:28:49,185 --> 00:28:50,854
- Wait a moment.
- Okay.

448
00:28:50,937 --> 00:28:51,771
Mm.

449
00:28:54,524 --> 00:28:55,358
Okay?

450
00:28:57,068 --> 00:28:57,902
Hey!

451
00:29:14,377 --> 00:29:15,754
Ah, uh…

452
00:29:15,837 --> 00:29:16,880
Good afternoon.

453
00:29:16,963 --> 00:29:18,214
Hello.

454
00:29:18,298 --> 00:29:19,591
Andrei.

455
00:29:19,674 --> 00:29:22,343
I hope you don't mind…
if we ask you a few questions.

456
00:29:36,483 --> 00:29:38,234
just sit down!

457
00:29:54,709 --> 00:29:55,668
Nine years ago,

458
00:29:56,503 --> 00:29:58,004
at the Harmonie Competition.

459
00:29:59,047 --> 00:30:01,633
Are you the one who abducted this man?

460
00:30:08,556 --> 00:30:09,682
Who the hell's asking?

461
00:30:15,647 --> 00:30:16,481
Oh…

462
00:30:17,774 --> 00:30:19,400
I remember you.

463
00:30:20,568 --> 00:30:23,822
You're the guy who won that competition,
right?

464
00:30:24,447 --> 00:30:28,117
The one who benefited the most from that…
mess.

465
00:30:31,079 --> 00:30:32,163
Let me ask you again.

466
00:30:33,915 --> 00:30:36,626
You abducted Jeong-yo Choi, right?

467
00:30:37,377 --> 00:30:38,378
What's in it for me?

468
00:30:44,717 --> 00:30:45,677
What did you do

469
00:30:46,511 --> 00:30:47,345
to Jeong-yo?

470
00:30:49,806 --> 00:30:50,640
He's dead.

471
00:30:53,351 --> 00:30:55,562
- Dead?
- Yes, dead.

472
00:30:58,189 --> 00:31:00,191
- By whom?
- Me.

473
00:31:05,530 --> 00:31:06,614
Why did you kill him?

474
00:31:09,659 --> 00:31:12,370
Why… did you kill him?

475
00:31:14,038 --> 00:31:15,039
It was not the plan.

476
00:31:15,540 --> 00:31:19,377
The plan was to let him go after
we got the money.

477
00:31:19,878 --> 00:31:21,087
But…

478
00:31:21,963 --> 00:31:24,132
he put up a bit too much of a fight.

479
00:31:24,215 --> 00:31:25,300
Was it for money?

480
00:31:25,383 --> 00:31:27,552
Did you abduct him for that reason?
Or did someone--

481
00:31:27,635 --> 00:31:28,469
Enough.

482
00:31:29,596 --> 00:31:30,471
You want to know?

483
00:31:32,682 --> 00:31:33,975
Three million lei.

484
00:31:35,393 --> 00:31:36,352
Then I'll tell you.

485
00:31:46,988 --> 00:31:48,865
- Tell me!
- Mister Kang, don't!

486
00:31:49,365 --> 00:31:51,451
You killed him for something so small?

487
00:31:51,534 --> 00:31:53,703
You know who he was? He was my friend!

488
00:31:53,786 --> 00:31:54,621
Come on, stop!

489
00:32:13,056 --> 00:32:14,682
Do you know who we are?

490
00:32:15,266 --> 00:32:16,100
You little…

491
00:32:17,936 --> 00:32:18,770
Huh?

492
00:32:19,604 --> 00:32:20,438
You know what?

493
00:32:21,230 --> 00:32:22,065
Now,

494
00:32:22,815 --> 00:32:23,858
six million.

495
00:32:24,901 --> 00:32:25,860
Then I'll tell you.

496
00:32:45,964 --> 00:32:46,798
Ugh…

497
00:32:53,763 --> 00:32:56,015
Is there an international bank close
by here?

498
00:32:56,808 --> 00:32:58,977
Huh? You wanna come back?

499
00:33:20,873 --> 00:33:22,458
Huh? Hold up.

500
00:33:22,959 --> 00:33:23,918
What's going on?

501
00:33:31,467 --> 00:33:32,301
Crap…

502
00:33:32,385 --> 00:33:35,346
Excuse me sir, you can’t come in here.
POLICE

503
00:33:35,430 --> 00:33:38,850
A man named Andrei has been killed.
Some kind of a fight.

504
00:33:46,691 --> 00:33:48,026
He tell you what happened?

505
00:33:50,194 --> 00:33:51,029
Andrei, uh…

506
00:33:52,113 --> 00:33:53,031
was just murdered.

507
00:33:54,032 --> 00:33:57,201
- I don't understand.
- Apparently there was some kind of fight…

508
00:33:57,285 --> 00:33:58,202
and he was killed.

509
00:33:59,954 --> 00:34:00,830
- No.
- Wait, Pi-o.

510
00:34:00,913 --> 00:34:02,665
Wait, don't be stupid!

511
00:34:04,250 --> 00:34:05,209
Wait! Pi-o, don't…!

512
00:34:05,793 --> 00:34:06,627
Hey…

513
00:34:07,295 --> 00:34:08,337
Stop, Stop Pi-o!

514
00:34:40,620 --> 00:34:41,537
Are you all right?

515
00:34:44,749 --> 00:34:46,417
Ah, guess my work here's done.

516
00:34:47,502 --> 00:34:49,170
I'm sure that Mister Choi is, uh…

517
00:34:50,004 --> 00:34:51,923
looking down from heaven with a smile.

518
00:34:52,465 --> 00:34:53,883
Knowing he had a friend

519
00:34:53,966 --> 00:34:56,177
who spent all this time searching
for him.

520
00:34:56,969 --> 00:34:58,012
Now that it's done…

521
00:34:59,597 --> 00:35:01,307
I hope you can let go of the dead.

522
00:35:04,811 --> 00:35:06,020
And find some happiness.

523
00:35:12,860 --> 00:35:14,195
Thank you for everything.

524
00:35:46,936 --> 00:35:48,437
Hey, Kang Pi-o!

525
00:35:48,980 --> 00:35:51,399
Where did you go?
How come your not back yet?

526
00:35:52,316 --> 00:35:55,027
You said you'd make time for U-hyeok,
but you haven't.

527
00:35:55,987 --> 00:35:57,196
Anyway, guess what?

528
00:35:57,280 --> 00:35:58,990
He made it to the semifinals.

529
00:36:00,408 --> 00:36:02,618
Where are you? You back in Berlin?

530
00:36:03,327 --> 00:36:04,162
No.

531
00:36:05,204 --> 00:36:06,539
I'm in Moldova…

532
00:36:07,331 --> 00:36:08,166
What?

533
00:36:08,249 --> 00:36:09,083
Moldova?

534
00:36:10,209 --> 00:36:11,043
Uh…

535
00:36:12,003 --> 00:36:13,963
What's wrong with your voice, you okay?

536
00:36:15,423 --> 00:36:16,257
Are you sick?

537
00:36:20,720 --> 00:36:21,554
Kang Pi-o!

538
00:36:23,514 --> 00:36:24,348
Hey…

539
00:36:24,891 --> 00:36:26,893
You can't just stay in bed like this.

540
00:36:27,810 --> 00:36:28,769
You need a doctor…

541
00:36:30,730 --> 00:36:31,898
I need a headache pill…

542
00:36:32,440 --> 00:36:34,233
- Huh?
- I just need a headache pill.

543
00:36:34,317 --> 00:36:35,359
That's it?

544
00:36:38,905 --> 00:36:39,739
Okay.

545
00:36:48,456 --> 00:36:49,832
Are you feeling better now?

546
00:36:53,669 --> 00:36:54,503
Uh-huh…

547
00:36:55,796 --> 00:36:56,631
Good…

548
00:36:59,008 --> 00:37:01,469
I brought you a little something to
eat as well.

549
00:37:01,552 --> 00:37:03,471
It doesn't look very good, but…

550
00:37:03,554 --> 00:37:04,513
you should eat.

551
00:37:04,597 --> 00:37:05,765
Even just a little bit.

552
00:37:06,891 --> 00:37:08,267
It'll give you some energy.

553
00:37:09,936 --> 00:37:10,770
Thanks.

554
00:37:26,035 --> 00:37:26,869
Sorry.

555
00:37:27,495 --> 00:37:28,329
Really

556
00:37:29,872 --> 00:37:30,706
So, uh…

557
00:37:31,832 --> 00:37:32,917
Wanna share?

558
00:37:33,000 --> 00:37:35,086
What were you doing all the way out here?

559
00:37:36,420 --> 00:37:37,255
Uh…

560
00:37:37,755 --> 00:37:39,840
is there something you're hiding from me?

561
00:37:41,759 --> 00:37:43,594
I came here hoping to meet Jeong-yo.

562
00:37:44,428 --> 00:37:45,263
Huh?

563
00:37:46,055 --> 00:37:48,140
I heard that the guy who kidnapped him,

564
00:37:48,849 --> 00:37:50,685
Got out of jail and was living here.

565
00:37:55,982 --> 00:37:56,857
And then?

566
00:37:57,692 --> 00:37:58,651
Jeong-yo's dead.

567
00:38:02,113 --> 00:38:03,614
He's been dead since that day.

568
00:38:05,992 --> 00:38:06,993
Nine years ago.

569
00:38:10,705 --> 00:38:12,540
I was hoping he was still alive.

570
00:38:14,166 --> 00:38:15,001
I hoped…

571
00:38:18,087 --> 00:38:20,047
I had really hoped that he wasn't dead.

572
00:38:22,049 --> 00:38:24,010
Now there's no way I'll be forgiven.

573
00:38:27,763 --> 00:38:29,265
There's no going back.

574
00:38:30,433 --> 00:38:32,268
It's time for you to move on.

575
00:38:33,102 --> 00:38:34,854
I mean, it happened so long ago. So why…

576
00:38:34,937 --> 00:38:37,106
Because I stole Jeong-yo's spot-light.

577
00:38:38,316 --> 00:38:40,693
Oh, why would you say something
like that, huh?

578
00:38:41,944 --> 00:38:43,738
You played really well that night.

579
00:38:44,613 --> 00:38:47,325
That's why no-one ever questioned
the judges decision.

580
00:38:48,451 --> 00:38:50,202
Even if Jeong-yo had played…

581
00:38:51,203 --> 00:38:52,121
you would've won.

582
00:38:53,205 --> 00:38:54,040
No.

583
00:38:57,293 --> 00:38:58,878
I'm sitting in Jeong-yo's spot.

584
00:39:00,296 --> 00:39:01,130
And now…

585
00:39:02,381 --> 00:39:04,342
I can't even set things right anymore.

586
00:39:23,986 --> 00:39:25,154
Why didn't you tell me?

587
00:39:27,448 --> 00:39:28,491
If you were hurting…

588
00:39:30,785 --> 00:39:32,536
Why didn't you at least tell me?

589
00:39:43,214 --> 00:39:45,424
Just let it go… Pi-o.

590
00:39:46,509 --> 00:39:47,343
We should…

591
00:39:49,136 --> 00:39:50,346
just let Jeong-yo go.

592
00:39:52,181 --> 00:39:53,099
I believe…

593
00:39:54,517 --> 00:39:56,143
that's what Jeong-yo would want.

594
00:40:00,022 --> 00:40:01,399
He would want you…

595
00:40:03,025 --> 00:40:05,403
to become an amazing
pianist in his place.

596
00:40:31,220 --> 00:40:33,097
I promise I will never leave you.

597
00:40:59,123 --> 00:41:00,458
Your plane's leaving soon.

598
00:41:02,001 --> 00:41:03,878
Don't go crying just cos you miss me.

599
00:41:06,338 --> 00:41:07,173
Hey.

600
00:41:08,174 --> 00:41:10,926
You really gonna keep making me feel this
is one-sided?

601
00:41:14,555 --> 00:41:15,389
I'll get going.

602
00:41:16,640 --> 00:41:17,475
Mm-hmm.

603
00:41:21,937 --> 00:41:22,771
Bye.

604
00:41:57,556 --> 00:41:58,390
Hey, kiddo!

605
00:41:59,725 --> 00:42:01,268
Here. I got it.

606
00:42:02,436 --> 00:42:04,980
I told you not to come pick me up,
why are you here?

607
00:42:05,064 --> 00:42:06,190
How could I not?

608
00:42:06,273 --> 00:42:08,234
I haven't seen you in six months, right?

609
00:42:08,317 --> 00:42:09,693
I miss you so much I cried.

610
00:42:10,611 --> 00:42:13,280
I saw the video of your gala in Prague.
You were great.

611
00:42:13,364 --> 00:42:14,281
Your Berlin Concert?

612
00:42:14,365 --> 00:42:15,407
How was it?

613
00:42:16,742 --> 00:42:17,576
Fine.

614
00:42:19,912 --> 00:42:21,497
Hey. Let me take that.

615
00:42:36,262 --> 00:42:37,555
Welcome home, Pi-o.

616
00:42:38,097 --> 00:42:39,306
I hope you've been well.

617
00:42:40,349 --> 00:42:42,643
His luggage is in the trunk. Could you
get it?

618
00:42:42,726 --> 00:42:43,727
Where's Mister Kang?

619
00:42:53,988 --> 00:42:54,822
Father.

620
00:42:55,614 --> 00:42:56,448
Pi-o is here.

621
00:43:04,290 --> 00:43:06,417
Hello Grandfather… how've you been?

622
00:43:13,841 --> 00:43:16,343
Your one and only grandson is back after
six months.

623
00:43:16,427 --> 00:43:18,012
Could you say something to him?

624
00:43:18,554 --> 00:43:19,471
You're in the way.

625
00:43:22,683 --> 00:43:24,602
Can you move? You're blocking my fan.

626
00:43:27,396 --> 00:43:28,230
Oh…

627
00:43:34,570 --> 00:43:35,404
Let's go.

628
00:43:43,537 --> 00:43:45,122
He's a stubborn old man.

629
00:43:45,205 --> 00:43:47,499
I thought he'd get better when he got
older…

630
00:43:47,583 --> 00:43:49,418
but he's just as stubborn as ever.

631
00:43:50,252 --> 00:43:51,462
Don't worry about me.

632
00:43:52,171 --> 00:43:53,047
I'm fine with it.

633
00:44:42,054 --> 00:44:44,139
PRAGUE HARMONIE INTERNATIONAL COMPETITION

634
00:44:56,151 --> 00:44:58,779
I'VE ALREADY MEMORIZED IT ALL
USE IT IF YOU NEED IT!

635
00:45:23,637 --> 00:45:24,763
Hi, Pi-o!

636
00:45:25,472 --> 00:45:26,890
Have you been well, Ms. Han?

637
00:45:27,474 --> 00:45:29,852
I haven't been well, because I
missed you.

638
00:45:30,436 --> 00:45:33,355
Going to see your performances was the
highlight of my days,

639
00:45:33,439 --> 00:45:35,065
but I've been too busy for that.

640
00:45:36,817 --> 00:45:39,153
Hey… You're looking a bit pale.

641
00:45:39,653 --> 00:45:40,946
Is something the matter?

642
00:45:41,989 --> 00:45:42,823
Not at all.

643
00:45:44,491 --> 00:45:46,410
Look, your album's out.

644
00:45:50,122 --> 00:45:50,956
What do you think?

645
00:45:51,039 --> 00:45:52,207
Came out nicely, right?

646
00:45:52,791 --> 00:45:53,625
Mm

647
00:45:54,626 --> 00:45:57,755
We should start planning your recital
tour to coincide with the album's

648
00:45:57,838 --> 00:45:58,672
release.

649
00:45:58,756 --> 00:46:00,674
Pi-o, what cities do you want to play?

650
00:46:01,467 --> 00:46:02,301
Well,

651
00:46:02,801 --> 00:46:03,677
the usual ones.

652
00:46:04,219 --> 00:46:05,053
Hmm…

653
00:46:05,637 --> 00:46:07,431
So, at minimum, Seoul, Incheon,

654
00:46:07,514 --> 00:46:08,724
Daejeon, Daegu, Busan,

655
00:46:09,224 --> 00:46:10,267
and Tongyeong.

656
00:46:10,350 --> 00:46:12,102
I think that'll be a nice tour.

657
00:46:12,186 --> 00:46:14,480
You agree? Too many at once?

658
00:46:14,563 --> 00:46:16,064
Should we just do four cities?

659
00:46:18,901 --> 00:46:19,735
No, it's good.

660
00:46:20,277 --> 00:46:21,195
It should be fine.

661
00:47:31,348 --> 00:47:33,517
LEDANOL

662
00:48:46,465 --> 00:48:47,299
Pi-o.

663
00:48:47,883 --> 00:48:49,760
KANG PI-O, GENIUS ON THE BRINK?
FIRST CRACK IN THE PERFECTIONIST'S ARMOR

664
00:48:49,843 --> 00:48:52,220
A MYSTERIOUS REPEATED PASSAGE
WHILE PERFORMING "GASPARD DE LA NUIT"…

665
00:48:52,304 --> 00:48:55,933
Please just open this door.
You haven't eaten anything in days!

666
00:48:58,310 --> 00:49:00,854
You've had so many event's lately and
you couldn't practice.

667
00:49:00,938 --> 00:49:03,357
You're just under the weather, that's all
it is.

668
00:49:03,440 --> 00:49:04,524
Just rest up.

669
00:49:04,608 --> 00:49:06,860
You're routine will help you back-- Oh…

670
00:49:11,490 --> 00:49:12,324
Pi…

671
00:49:45,857 --> 00:49:46,692
Pi-o.

672
00:49:48,527 --> 00:49:49,361
Mr. Do.

673
00:49:52,447 --> 00:49:53,573
I'm all messed up…

674
00:49:55,659 --> 00:49:56,493
And you still…

675
00:49:58,203 --> 00:49:59,746
can't stand to see my face?

676
00:50:03,583 --> 00:50:05,335
I waited for you for so long…

677
00:50:07,671 --> 00:50:08,672
and you avoid me?

678
00:50:13,218 --> 00:50:14,052
Why?

679
00:50:16,346 --> 00:50:20,100
Are you uncomfortable around me now cos
of my mom, or is it something else?

680
00:50:21,184 --> 00:50:23,979
Is it because I was never a good enough
student for you?

681
00:50:24,062 --> 00:50:25,522
What are you talking about? That's not
true.

682
00:50:25,605 --> 00:50:26,440
No, uh…

683
00:50:27,816 --> 00:50:30,277
Can you… Just be honest with me.

684
00:50:31,111 --> 00:50:33,530
Did you ever really consider me
your student, Mister Do?

685
00:50:33,613 --> 00:50:35,490
Pi-o, what are you talking about?

686
00:50:35,574 --> 00:50:36,700
I've always, uh…

687
00:50:38,660 --> 00:50:40,412
wanted to ask you this.

688
00:50:41,663 --> 00:50:44,332
Why did you make me play the same piece
as Jeong-yo?

689
00:50:45,250 --> 00:50:46,084
What?

690
00:50:46,168 --> 00:50:49,546
I told you that I wanted to play Rach
Three, so why did you make me play

691
00:50:49,629 --> 00:50:52,215
Rach Two?
Did you do that to me on purpose?

692
00:50:52,299 --> 00:50:54,217
So everyone could see how much
better he was?

693
00:50:54,301 --> 00:50:56,928
Pi-o, I'm afraid that's a terrible
misunderstanding.

694
00:50:58,055 --> 00:50:59,181
Both you and Jeong-yo

695
00:50:59,264 --> 00:51:00,557
were equally precious.

696
00:51:01,850 --> 00:51:03,643
Both of you were so important to me.

697
00:51:03,727 --> 00:51:06,813
Then why is it you're always giving me
such a cold shoulder?

698
00:51:07,439 --> 00:51:11,276
You know I've always counted on your
guidance and your help, so… why…

699
00:51:12,819 --> 00:51:15,113
Why is there only room in your heart
for the one who's gone?

700
00:51:15,197 --> 00:51:16,406
No. That's not true.

701
00:51:19,451 --> 00:51:20,911
My heart breaks for you, too.

702
00:51:21,661 --> 00:51:22,496
And I'm worried.

703
00:51:24,790 --> 00:51:27,751
But, now, there's really nothing left
for me to teach you

704
00:51:29,669 --> 00:51:32,547
because you've become a pianist
with a voice of your own.

705
00:51:33,632 --> 00:51:35,759
I thought the best thing I could do was…

706
00:51:36,843 --> 00:51:39,054
to quietly cheer you
on from the sidelines.

707
00:51:39,137 --> 00:51:40,347
That's not true!

708
00:51:41,598 --> 00:51:42,933
You've always hated me!

709
00:51:44,643 --> 00:51:47,521
Hey, just admit that I'm a student
that you never wanted!

710
00:51:48,063 --> 00:51:50,774
You know I'm an amateur hack and have
ZERO talent!

711
00:51:51,358 --> 00:51:53,819
Say you couldn't stand having
a pathetic student…

712
00:51:54,402 --> 00:51:56,321
who played music without ANY SOUL!

713
00:52:00,242 --> 00:52:01,076
Ah…

714
00:52:23,014 --> 00:52:24,015
KANG PI-O RECITAL

715
00:52:24,099 --> 00:52:25,308
THE CRACKS DIDN'T START ON STAGE

716
00:52:25,392 --> 00:52:27,644
PIANIST KANG PI-O'S DOWNFALL
WAS INEVITABLE

717
00:52:37,154 --> 00:52:38,947
Kang Pi-o, get up, now.

718
00:52:39,447 --> 00:52:41,241
Jae-in's here, so get up.

719
00:52:42,826 --> 00:52:44,035
I said you have a guest-

720
00:52:58,717 --> 00:52:59,551
Pi-o.

721
00:53:01,178 --> 00:53:02,512
Come on, sit up here.

722
00:53:12,355 --> 00:53:13,190
So…

723
00:53:14,107 --> 00:53:16,484
How long are you going
to keep doing this?

724
00:53:16,568 --> 00:53:19,070
So you ruined one show - Is your life
finished?

725
00:53:20,030 --> 00:53:21,406
The deeper you let yourself sink,

726
00:53:21,489 --> 00:53:23,992
the harder it is to find the
surface again, right?

727
00:53:24,576 --> 00:53:25,410
I'm sorry…

728
00:53:27,037 --> 00:53:28,163
Just leave me alone.

729
00:53:29,873 --> 00:53:31,208
I'll be fine on my own.

730
00:53:31,791 --> 00:53:34,044
Look, instead of staying here in Korea,

731
00:53:34,127 --> 00:53:35,837
why don't you go travel somewhere?

732
00:53:36,671 --> 00:53:39,841
I know it's harder for you to stay here
with all the rumors, the prying eyes,

733
00:53:39,925 --> 00:53:40,967
and everything else.

734
00:53:41,801 --> 00:53:44,554
Take that trip around Europe
you've always wanted to do.

735
00:53:44,638 --> 00:53:46,264
It might help clear your head.

736
00:53:48,433 --> 00:53:49,809
Where am I going to hide?

737
00:53:51,353 --> 00:53:53,980
Nothing changes the fact I can't play the
piano.

738
00:53:54,064 --> 00:53:56,024
There's nowhere I can hide from it.

739
00:54:03,782 --> 00:54:05,700
LEE BO-HUN

740
00:54:07,994 --> 00:54:10,330
I kept seeing what looked like the ghost
of---

741
00:54:11,498 --> 00:54:12,415
my missing friend.

742
00:54:13,875 --> 00:54:16,586
I thought that if I held some kind of
funeral for him,

743
00:54:17,295 --> 00:54:18,672
I'd finally get better.

744
00:54:19,506 --> 00:54:20,966
But now I feel like…

745
00:54:22,467 --> 00:54:23,677
I'm sinking under water…

746
00:54:25,845 --> 00:54:26,930
Cos I know he's dead.

747
00:54:27,889 --> 00:54:29,015
Uh, maybe

748
00:54:29,641 --> 00:54:33,061
it's because you never gave yourself the
time to properly mourn him.

749
00:54:33,645 --> 00:54:34,688
Hm, perhaps…

750
00:54:35,397 --> 00:54:38,316
you could take a little time to properly
face your grief?

751
00:54:39,067 --> 00:54:39,901
Accepting it…

752
00:54:40,485 --> 00:54:43,029
and letting it go is the best way to move
forward.

753
00:55:42,297 --> 00:55:43,757
Yeah me too.

754
00:55:43,840 --> 00:55:44,924
Should we go inside?

755
00:55:45,008 --> 00:55:46,384
Yeah, let's find our seats.

756
00:58:26,461 --> 00:58:29,297
SPECIAL THANKS TO KO CHANG-SEOK
FOR HIS GUEST APPEARANCE

757
00:58:49,692 --> 00:58:51,444
FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

758
00:58:51,945 --> 00:58:54,072
Today's winner, Luca Domenico.

759
00:58:54,572 --> 00:58:56,449
Choi Jeong-yo has returned.

760
00:58:56,533 --> 00:59:00,328
I do not wish for my music to be…
overshadowed by my past.

761
00:59:01,329 --> 00:59:03,581
There's no way I wouldn't recognize you.

762
00:59:03,665 --> 00:59:05,083
It's definitely Jeong-yo.

763
00:59:05,875 --> 00:59:08,211
Choi Jeong-yo! Please, let me see him.

764
00:59:08,294 --> 00:59:10,547
Mr. Domenico says he doesn't know you.

765
00:59:10,630 --> 00:59:12,298
I have another favor to ask.

766
00:59:13,550 --> 00:59:14,384
GENERATIVE AI TECHNOLOGY
WAS USED IN SOME SCENES.

767
00:59:14,467 --> 00:59:17,136
Look into it.
Dig into it without anyone finding out.
